Subject: Hijack the online multiplayer menu to the debug LAN multiplayer
Upstream-base: f75ccf1ad20e5bd7585962990db08067c0ae498a

Retail never calls NetworkSession::InitializeLAN. Under the explicit
MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_LAN admission, Main Menu's Online item starts
the LAN session and pushes the original lobby (scene 24, NetworkStartScene)
instead of the DWC login; its back button shuts the session down and returns
to Main Menu. The lobby and the two network draft scenes leave their gated
blocks, split only at case boundaries; hub, login, Mii selection and every
DWC scene keep their gates. After a LAN match the frontend returns to Main
Menu like a friendly match instead of pushing the unadmitted online hub.

The admission prints the original DC_NETWORK debug channel to stderr.
SHOnlinePlayerCount's button context words are narrowed through
std::uintptr_t natively.

diff --git a/include/Game/Sys/debug.h b/include/Game/Sys/debug.h
index 11f42ad..8b3a9c2 100644
--- a/include/Game/Sys/debug.h
+++ b/include/Game/Sys/debug.h
@@ -1,6 +1,11 @@
 #ifndef _DEBUG_H_
 #define _DEBUG_H_
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE) && defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_LAN)
+#include <cstdarg>
+#include <cstdio>
+#endif
+
 enum eDEBUG_CHANNEL
 {
     DC_STARTUP = 0,
@@ -31,6 +36,18 @@ namespace tDebugPrintManager
 
 inline int Print(eDEBUG_CHANNEL channel, const char* format, ...)
 {
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE) && defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_LAN)
+    // Retail strips debug output. The LAN admission keeps the original network
+    // channel, printed to stderr and so also kept in the session log.
+    if (channel == DC_NETWORK)
+    {
+        va_list args;
+        va_start(args, format);
+        std::fputs("[net] ", stderr);
+        std::vfprintf(stderr, format, args);
+        va_end(args);
+    }
+#endif
     return channel;
 }
 
